---
import { RELAY_README } from "../data/links";
---

<section class="section relay" aria-labelledby="relay-title">
    <div class="wrap relay-grid">
        <div class="section-head">
            <h2 id="relay-title">Your relay, or none</h2>
            <p>
                On one network nothing else is needed. Across the internet, two machines behind
                strict routers need a server to meet at. Run the relay image yourself, or pass
                <code translate="no">--n0-relays</code> to use n0's public relays.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="relay-body">
            <dl class="relay-modes">
                <div>
                    <dt>Meeting point</dt>
                    <dd>Coordinates the hole punch at 64 KiB/s per client and carries no file data.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>Full relay</dt>
                    <dd>Also carries the bytes for pairs that cannot connect directly.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
            <div class="relay-code">
                <pre translate="no"><code>docker pull ghcr.io/sanamhub/sluice-relay:0.1.0</code></pre>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">
                It ships closed, with an empty allowlist, so nobody uses it until you add an endpoint
                id. The <a href={RELAY_README}>relay README</a> has the certificate, both recipes and
                the guard that checks its config.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
